:KyQ_SbaGAqAAaQt_ a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description "Political offices were different bodies. “In Athens, for example, citizens had the right to attend the assembly, the council, and other bodies, or to sit on juries. The Athenian system differed from a modern representative democracy in that the citizens were more directly involved in governing.” (Miller)" ;
