:GpKECZaAUcEwZghM a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description """The efficient cause: ‘the primary source of the change or rest’, e.g., the artisan, the art of bronze-casting the statue, the man who gives advice, the father of the child. […] However, an adequate explanation of the production of a statue requires also a reference to the efficient cause or the principle that produces the statue. For Aristotle, this principle is the art of bronze-casting the statue (Phys. 195 a 6–8. Cf. Metaph. 1013 b 6–9).” (Falcon) 
Efficient cause, or the means by which it is the object created.""" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
    ontouml:isExtensional false ;
    ontouml:isPowertype false ;
    ontouml:name "EfficientCause"@en ;
    ontouml:order "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    ontouml:project :8evc5z6GAqACBh.w ;
    ontouml:restrictedTo ontouml:functionalComplexNature ;
    ontouml:stereotype ontouml:subkind .

