:BkRNSbaGAqAAaQna a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description "\"Polis, the city-state is composed of individual citizens, who, along with natural resources, are the ‘material’ or ‘equipment’ out of which the city-state is fashioned… the city-state is a hylomorphic (i.e., matter-form) compound of a particular population (i.e., citizen-body) in a given territory (material cause) and a constitution (formal cause).” (Miller)" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
