:sUsECZaAUcEwZggp a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description """“The material cause: ‘that out of which’, e.g., the bronze of a statue. […] The bronze enters in the explanation of the production of the statue as the material cause. Note that the bronze is not only the material out of which the statue is made; it is also the subject of change, that is, the thing that undergoes the change and results in a statue. The bronze is melted and poured in order to acquire a new shape, the shape of the statue.” (Falcon) 
Material causes are the elements out of which an object is created.""" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
    ontouml:isExtensional false ;
    ontouml:isPowertype false ;
    ontouml:name "MaterialCause"@en ;
    ontouml:order "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    ontouml:project :8evc5z6GAqACBh.w ;
    ontouml:restrictedTo ontouml:functionalComplexNature ;
    ontouml:stereotype ontouml:subkind .

