:C6GfoPaGAqAAagyg a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description "Aristotle distinguishes two kinds of virtue: “those that pertain to the part of the soul that engages in reasoning (virtues of mind or intellect), and those that pertain to the part of the soul that cannot itself reason but is nonetheless capable of following reason (ethical virtues, virtues of character).” (Kraut)" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
