:uAl.BZaAUcEY.Qhe a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description """A material object. 
“‘ordinary objects’ … as a first approximation, it serves to rely on the sorts of examples Aristotle himself employs when motivating hylomorphism: statues and houses, horses and humans." (Shields) 
Objects are essential particulars, like statues and houses, horses, and humans. 
Objects, according to Aristotle are primary existents, compounds of Matter and Form.""" ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
    ontouml:isPowertype false ;
    ontouml:name "Object"@en ;
    ontouml:order "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    ontouml:project :8evc5z6GAqACBh.w ;
    ontouml:restrictedTo ontouml:functionalComplexNature ;
    ontouml:stereotype ontouml:kind .

